      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Concepts on the go \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Concepts on the go \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Y3jegDnt_wNByJWdgpEyA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1673.2154827223335,
      "y": 107.34635044739571,
      "width": 936.6849612241604,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526339248,
      "version": 5846,
      "versionNonce": 1275447154,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764505781509,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Text based Search is best done with elastic search. Why? \n    - Inverted Index \n    - Distributed Architecture & Scalable \n    - Relevance scoring algos on results \n    - Stores data as schema-free JSON documents\n2) Proximity Search: searching for restaurants, hotels or something based on the location.\nThere are 4 ways of doing this efficiently. \n    a) Elastic Search: Uses geo data and Indexing- internally uses quad trees & geo hashing.  \n    b) Quad Trees: \n    c) PostGres DB with GIS extension\n    d) GeoHash\n3) SQL data bases are picked based on the strong relationships/tables or based on ACID\nproperties for distributed transactions. \n4) Whenever we are doing something event driven where multiple actions are interlinked we use a\nmessage queue -- kafka. Like for the case of order where first we go to the payment gateway \nthen we notify the user about order begin successfully placed and then to the restaurant. \n\n\n\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Text based Search is best done with elastic search. Why? \n    - Inverted Index \n    - Distributed Architecture & Scalable \n    - Relevance scoring algos on results \n    - Stores data as schema-free JSON documents\n2) Proximity Search: searching for restaurants, hotels or something based on the location.  There are 4 ways of doing this efficiently. \n    a) Elastic Search: Uses geo data and Indexing- internally uses quad trees & geo hashing.  \n    b) Quad Trees: \n    c) PostGres DB with GIS extension\n    d) GeoHash\n3) SQL data bases are picked based on the strong relationships/tables or based on ACID properties for distributed transactions. \n4) Whenever we are doing something event driven where multiple actions are interlinked we use a message queue -- kafka. Like for the case of order where first we go to the payment gateway \nthen we notify the user about order begin successfully placed and then to the restaurant. \n\n\n\n    ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
